# Accepted gap for 32-decorator-application. A NEW missing edge fails the suite; a line
# here that STARTS working also fails, so the debt cannot rot.
#
# PARSER-BLOCKED, and the engine cannot close it. A bare `@guarded` gets a ts_decorator
# row with kind = MARKER and NO ts_call_site, so the application is absent from the IR
# entirely. The engine has no site to attach an edge to, and score.py joins the oracle to
# IR call sites by position — so the compiler's row becomes CONSERVATION LOSS and leaves
# the denominator rather than counting as a miss. Nothing in the rules can recover that;
# it needs a call site emitted. parser#82, and #233 for the measurement.
#
# The FACTORY form beside it is the control and resolves: `@timed()` does emit a call
# site for the factory call, which is what makes this attributable to the bare form and
# not to decorators in general.
#
# This case is also the first in the suite to use a decorator at all. Until #233 the case
# oracle's node list omitted `ts.isDecorator` while the project oracle emitted
# DECORATOR_CALL, so the per-case suite was green on decorators whatever the engine did.
# Both sides now say the same thing, which is why this line can exist.
Svc#a() -> svc#guarded(unknown,string,PropertyDescriptor)
